17230	{"artifactId":"LLD-b9d5c5c40df5a574-s7","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-b9d5c5c40df5a574-s7-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:34:17.731Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion of Define Story S007 (ac1 complete to a final report, ac2 nested plans, ac3 a stopped run says where and why, ac4 a completed run is replayed) is designed, and the docs-family gap on ac1 is an exception recorded upstream rather than a silent omission.","evidence":"DEF.md:236-239 lists ac1-ac4 exactly as the design maps them (section 6 acceptance mapping covers all four). The docs exception is recorded in the Define itself: DEF.md:55 'S003:FR005 — ... this closes the exception accepted on Story s7 for the docs family' and DEF.md:167 (S003 ac7) 'where Story s7 was accepted with that analysis not completing'. The module notion is split to S008 (DEF.md:241), which the design leaves alone. [files: docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today one missing input skips the aggregate task and the run fails with 'executor-aggregator-failed'; an aggregate task with an empty consumes list always runs with no upstream output.","evidence":"walker.ts:133-157 skips any task for which unmetDependencies returns a name, with no exception for the aggregator; unmetDependencies (walker.ts:329-346) returns the first consumed name not in outputs and null for an empty list; projectUpstream (354-365) iterates only `task.consumes ?? []`. driver.ts:385-404 fails the run with 'executor-aggregator-failed' when rootPlan.finalReport is undefined. executePlannerTask (walker.ts:299-303) fails the planner task when the child has no report, so the child-plan claim follows too. [files: src/analyze/executor/walker.ts, src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An error nothing catches leaves the run record 'in-progress', and the daemon's handler reports stage 'classify' whatever stage was running.","evidence":"driver.ts:147-156 writes the first record with status 'in-progress'; the resume read (133) and `await runExecutor(...)` (359) and completeRun (409) sit outside any try, as do the walk's writeTaskOutput calls (walker.ts:144, 176). analyze-rpc.ts:542-558 catches a throw from runAnalyze and sends `stage: 'classify'` with 'internal-error' and writes no record. [files: src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts, src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts, src/analyze/executor/walker.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The plan tasks accept fewer kinds than TARGET_TO_KINDS and refuse with a plain Error; the pairing check is written twice (stepScope always, prepareScope in run mode only); the indexed check is made for the code source only.","evidence":"code/_shared.ts:58-69 accepts 'repo' and 'manifest-dir' and throws `new Error(... not supported yet ...)`; infra/_shared.ts:49-61 adds 'workspace'; data/_shared.ts:26-42 accepts workspace/repo/manifest-dir and no connection. TARGET_TO_KINDS (classifier/validate.ts:54-60) has the rows the design quotes. mcp/analyze-step/scope.ts:28-34 checks then resolves; context/driver.ts:1108-1114 checks only when `invocationMode === 'run' && 'intent' in inputs`; context/driver.ts:379 runs ensureNonEmptyClosure only when `invocationMode === 'run' && shaperId === 'code'`. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/code/_shared.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/infra/_shared.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/data/_shared.ts, src/analyze/context/driver.ts, src/mcp/analyze-step/scope.ts, src/analyze/classifier/validate.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon refuses an empty prompt even with a stated source, accepts a prompt of only white space, and an empty prompt with a stated source already gives an unfocused intent further in.","evidence":"analyze-rpc.ts:1066 `userPrompt: requireString(obj, 'userPrompt')`, and requireString (1284-1290) throws only on `v.length === 0` ('must be a non-empty string'), so white space passes. driver.ts:553-556 hintedIntentBase: `const focus = userPrompt.trim(); ... focus.length > 0 ? { focused: true, focus } : { target, focused: false, scopeRef }`. [files: src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts, src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"What the design calls new does not exist (resolveTaskScope, resolveScopeForTarget, isRunLive, absentInputs), and 'run-abandoned' is declared in both code lists and raised nowhere.","evidence":"A search of src (tests excluded) for resolveTaskScope|resolveScopeForTarget|isRunLive finds nothing; absentInputs has no match in src/analyze/executor. 'run-abandoned' appears only at orchestrator/types.ts:296 and analyze-rpc.ts:151 and :960 (the two lists), with no raise site. [files: src/analyze/orchestrator/types.ts, src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused pieces have the stated shape: resolveScope/ResolvedScope/ScopeDeps, the leniency of ensureNonEmptyClosure, and the symbol scope's stricter behaviour.","evidence":"context/scope.ts:43-68 gives ResolvedScope { repoPath: string|null, lookupPath, filePath?, entityId?, connectionId? } and ScopeDeps with listRepos() and listEntitiesForRepo(repoPath), so Pick<ScopeDeps,'listRepos'|'listEntitiesForRepo'> fits the two reads in invariants.ts:126 and :172. invariants.ts:108-110 takes only `scope` today; 125-151 returns undefined when the registry read throws or is empty; 162-178 throws ScopeNotIndexedError otherwise. scope.ts:168-172 resolveSymbol calls deps.listRepos() with no try and throws ScopeNotIndexedError when no repo contains the file; path kinds use lookupPath = ref.value (86-91). [files: src/analyze/context/scope.ts, src/analyze/context/invariants.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The inventory of scope readers is complete: three per-family functions with their callers, and five direct readers of the scope's value (adherence in two places).","evidence":"A search for resolveRepoPath|resolveRepoPathFromIntent|scopeRef\\.value under src/analyze/runtimes finds: code/_shared.ts:58 (used by structure-module-tree, discovery-entrypoints, discovery-modules, and docs/discovery-inventory.ts:39), infra/_shared.ts:49 (six infra tasks), data/_shared.ts:26 (discovery-objects, schema-table, discovery-connections); direct readers docs/family-summarise.ts:131, docs/constraint-enumerate.ts:45, docs/decision-trace.ts:46, shared/adherence.ts:219 and :376, and data/discovery-connections.ts:59-60 (`explicit ?? resolveRepoPathFromIntent`). The test hook is discovery-modules.ts:97. No other runtime reads the value. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/code/_shared.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/shared/adherence.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/data/discovery-connections.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each document runner shares one argument type with its prepare function and builds prepare's arguments field by field; prepare is what calls retrieval; the lookup pipeline calls prepare directly; the vector pass searches the whole repository and drops non-candidates; the vector filter short-circuits an empty list.","evidence":"doc-constraint-enumerate.ts:112-122 builds `{ subject, repoPath, db, ...maxSources, ...runId, ...logContext }` for prepareDocConstraintEnumerate(args: RunDocConstraintEnumerateArgs) (194-196), which calls retrieveDocSections at 206-214; doc-decision-trace.ts:117-127 and :207 are the same. explore/executor.ts:328 and :351 call the two prepare functions directly. docs-retrieval.ts:189-200 calls searchEntityVecs(..., { kinds }) then `if (!candidateById.has(h.id)) continue`. entity-vec.ts:297-301 EntityVecFilter is 'all'|'code'|'artifact'|{ kinds }, and 319-322 returns [] for an empty kinds list because 'DataFusion backend rejects `kind IN ()`'. [files: src/analyze/explore/doc-constraint-enumerate.ts, src/analyze/explore/doc-decision-trace.ts, src/analyze/explore/executor.ts, src/analyze/docs-retrieval.ts, src/db/lance/entity-vec.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Runs are started only in the daemon process, and the run record has exactly the three readers named (resume check, status request, purge), so an in-memory count in the daemon knows every live run.","evidence":"A search for `runAnalyze(` outside tests finds one caller: daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:541. `readRunRecord(` is called at orchestrator/driver.ts:133 (resume), orchestrator/persistence.ts:94 (purgeRun) and daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:762 (runStatus); no MCP or CLI code starts a run or reads a record directly. [files: src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts, src/analyze/orchestrator/persistence.ts, src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"There are five aggregate-report runtimes, all going through runAggregator with RunAggregatorArgs, so one prompt change and a pass-through in five files carries absentInputs.","evidence":"`runAggregator(` is called from runtimes/code, docs, infra, data and generic aggregate-report.ts and nowhere else; each passes `upstreamOutputs: args.upstreamOutputs` (code/aggregate-report.ts:41-48). aggregator.ts:52-68 defines RunAggregatorArgs, and renderUpstreamSection (178-197) is the one place the user message lists outputs, so a section after it is a single edit. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/shared/aggregator.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/code/aggregate-report.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding an optional `code` to the failed-task record and to tasksFailed entries needs no rewrite of stored records, and a resumed run reads older records as they are.","evidence":"executor/types.ts:142 `tasksFailed: ReadonlyArray<{ taskId: string; reason: string }>` and 145-160 TaskExecutionRecord have only optional trailing fields, so one more optional field is additive. driver.ts:514-527 resumedResult returns `cached.tasksFailed ?? []` and reads no per-entry field; RunRecord gains no field. I did not check the IDE repository's mirrored types (not in this repo); the design states they need the optional field. [files: src/analyze/executor/types.ts, src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts]","action":"None in this repository; the mirrored IDE type is a follow-up outside it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The liveness mechanism the design builds is the one its chosen alternative (8.1) and the HLD describe.","evidence":"HLD.md:39 states the mechanism: 'the daemon keeps, in memory, the set of run ids it is executing ... The three readers apply the rule: the status request ..., the purge ...' and the resume check. The design's own section 8.1 (CHOSEN) repeats that: 'The daemon keeps an in-memory set of running ids. Each of the three readers of a run record (the resume check, the status request, purgeRun) ... rewrites the record as failed with run-abandoned'. But section 2.3 says 'Liveness is a count of running runs per id, not a set of ids' and 'The resume check itself is unchanged', and section 3.3 says only two readers rewrite and the resume check 'makes none'. The contract sections give reasons for both departures and they are sound against the code (driver.ts:133-156 overwrites any non-completed record), but 8.1 was not brought in line and no HLD amendment is named for the departure from the HLD's stated set and third reader. [files: docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/HLD.md, docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/S007/LLD.md]","action":"Rewrite section 8.1 to say a count per id and two rewriting readers, with the resume check replacing the record; and record the departure from HLD line 39 as an amendment (or a note the HLD owner accepts), so the plan and build do not follow the stale text.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The three typed scope errors exist and both mapping functions already map them, with { scopePath, registeredAs } attached to 'scope-not-indexed' in both, so a shared function can return the code and that data without changing either result.","evidence":"invariants.ts:49-85 defines ScopeRefUnresolvedError, ScopeKindTargetMismatchError and ScopeNotIndexedError (with scopePath, registeredAs). orchestrator/driver.ts:606-612, 628-629 and daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:900-908, 933-937 each map the three, both attaching `data: { scopePath, registeredAs }` for not-indexed. The walk today catches a runtime throw as `failedRecord(task, 'runtime-threw: ' + msg)` (walker.ts:233-237) with no class check, so the coded failure is detectable at that one catch. driver.ts imports the executor (line 67), so placing the shared mapping in invariants.ts avoids the walk importing the driver. [files: src/analyze/context/invariants.ts, src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts, src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts, src/analyze/executor/walker.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A name the aggregate task consumes that no task produces is rejected by plan validation, and the abandoned and purge paths are detectable where the design puts them.","evidence":"planner/validate.ts:193-203 (INV-7) rejects 'consumes=... is not produced by any earlier task', and 478-499 repeats it for order. persistence.ts:87-100 purgeRun refuses a record with status 'in-progress' unless forced and returns { ok:false, code:'run-in-progress', stage }, which analyze-rpc.ts:799-821 relays; runStatus (752-777) returns the record as read, so both are single places for the liveness rule. [files: src/analyze/planner/validate.ts, src/analyze/orchestrator/persistence.ts, src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to a named test, and the existing tests the design says it replaces exist where it says.","evidence":"Section 6's acceptance mapping gives ac1 three tests (integration, live, unit), ac2 two, ac3 three, ac4 one, matching DEF.md:236-239. The tests to be replaced are present: matches for _resolveRepoPathForTest|resolveRepoPathFromIntent|resolveRepoPath|'not supported yet' are found in runtimes/code/__tests__/discovery-modules.test.ts (9), runtimes/data/__tests__/data-runtimes.test.ts (9) and runtimes/infra/__tests__/infra-runtimes.test.ts (4), and in no other test file under src/analyze. The walk already exports test hooks (_unmetDependenciesForTest, walker.ts:437). ac2's live proof is left as the design's own open question; I did not run any test. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/code/__tests__/discovery-modules.test.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/data/__tests__/data-runtimes.test.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/infra/__tests__/infra-runtimes.test.ts]","action":"Settle the open question on ac2 (whether the nested integration test stands as proof) before the plan stage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":15,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-08T13:34:17.731Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
